**Given:**

sin (cos⁻¹ dfrac{3}{5}) + cos (tan⁻¹ dfrac{5}{12})

**Formula used:**

If theta = cos⁻¹ dfrac{3}{5}, then sin theta = sqrt{1 - (dfrac{3}{5})²} 

If phi = tan⁻¹ dfrac{5}{12}, then cos phi = dfrac{12}{sqrt{12² + 5²}} 

**Calculation:**

sin (cos⁻¹ dfrac{3}{5}) = sqrt{1 - (dfrac{3}{5})²} 

⇒ sin (cos⁻¹ dfrac{3}{5}) = sqrt{1 - dfrac{9}{25}} 

⇒ sin (cos⁻¹ dfrac{3}{5}) = sqrt{dfrac{16}{25}} 

⇒ sin (cos⁻¹ dfrac{3}{5}) = dfrac{4}{5} 

cos (tan⁻¹ dfrac{5}{12}) = dfrac{12}{sqrt{12² + 5²}} 

⇒ cos (tan⁻¹ dfrac{5}{12}) = dfrac{12}{sqrt{144 + 25}} 

⇒ cos (tan⁻¹ dfrac{5}{12}) = dfrac{12}{sqrt{169}} 

⇒ cos (tan⁻¹ dfrac{5}{12}) = dfrac{12}{13} 

sin (cos⁻¹ dfrac{3}{5}) + cos (tan⁻¹ dfrac{5}{12}) 

⇒ dfrac{4}{5} + dfrac{12}{13} 

⇒ dfrac{4 times 13 + 12 times 5}{5 times 13} 

⇒ dfrac{52 + 60}{65} 

⇒ dfrac{112}{65} 

**∴ The correct answer is option (3).**
